Replaced the linear message scan with a lazily built 65536-entry direct lookup table, mapping each message number to the first matching `MESG` entry. After a tiny one-time initialization this makes `GetMesg` constant-time while preserving duplicate and NULL behavior exactly.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* table[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = static_cast<int>(MESGS) - 1; i >= 0; --i)
        {
            table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```